The isolated replay uses the shipped `openclaw.mjs` launcher and freshly built Gateway, actual SQLite broker saturation/release, the production startup owner, real ACP manager/acpx, a controlled maintained stdio ACP peer, and independent read-only SQLite history. It does not replace startup opening or publication callbacks. The candidate recovers the target without restarting again and retains seed history, session ID, configuration and workspace bytes. No live provider, Telegram, fleet performance, Linux, PostgreSQL runtime or new upgrade proof is claimed.

