## AI Assistance

Prepared with AI assistance (Codex); current canonical static review used Codex. Runtime proof and verification scope, failures and limits are stated above.

## What Problem This Solves

`openclaw connect <join-url>` keeps waiting when the root CLI accepts Ctrl-C or SIGTERM during a stalled join HTTP lookup. Its independent 15-second request deadline does not observe the invocation's cancellation signal, including while reading an incomplete JSON response.

Closes #187245.

## User Impact

Accepted interruption stops the owned join HTTP read and returns through root cleanup with 130/143. It does not print a late ordinary join error or admit a late join result to the node runtime. Completed responses retain their existing validation and diagnostic behavior. All join-URL option combinations share this private HTTP preflight owner.

## Why This Change Was Made

Pass the existing invocation work signal to the current guarded fetch and bounded response reader. Keep the existing deadline and finally-release owner, and check for accepted cancellation after release before runtime handoff. This uses one private lookup owner and adds no process signal handler, timer/controller, SDK surface, option, dependency or state format.

Target-file handling, direct setup-code runtime behavior and downstream service bootstrap/hosting-consent/installation are unchanged. The single-use join contract remains: cancellation cannot restore a code already redeemed at the Gateway.

