## What Problem This Solves

Closes #182410

Creating a quick diagram or spatial instruction currently requires a separate drawing app, an export, and an attachment import. The composer has no blank-canvas input.

## User Impact

Add **Draw a sketch** to the existing attachment menu. Draw, undo or clear, then attach a plain 800×450 PNG. It remains a draft until the user sends it. Blank/Clear disables Attach; Cancel and Escape leave the message unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

Reuse the existing annotation painter, native promise-modal lifecycle, and ordinary attachment admission/payload owners. A sketch is an ordinary image without browser screenshot context. The current plugin composer contract cannot stage a file into the built-in composer.

The current main menu split is preserved, including native mobile file selection and media inputs. Its attachment rows and selection handling now share one focused module; this keeps the main menu body below its existing 700-line limit. Sketch code loads only on invocation. No backend, settings, protocol or persisted format changes.

10 files; production +405/−95 and tests +83/−1 lines. **Product placement still needs a Control UI owner decision:** this PR proposes a built-in composer attachment action; it does not claim that design has been accepted.

## Evidence

