The complete production tree is unchanged from validated head `9cb13362ddd440b1e104f036759d24c4f92f5bb5`; only that one test expectation changed. Reused checks at that recorded SHA: 28/28 sketch/composer/painter tests (25.475 s), 39/39 Vite catalog tests (23.431 s), full UI types (160.404 s), focused typed lint/format, controller ratchets against pinned main, and i18n baseline/verify. Current test-only change passes focused lint/format and diff checks. No assertions, performance budgets or baselines were relaxed.

**Build/performance:** Native UI build, precompressed assets, and the unchanged performance gate pass at `9cb13362ddd440b1e104f036759d24c4f92f5bb5` against same-machine frozen main `a4e20a8b24440efd9b8a1792ce400be85a697080`. These results are reused because current production files and dependencies are byte-identical. Chat boot gzip: 1,275,239 → 1,275,038 B (−201 B); New Session: 778,690 → 778,511 B (−179 B); CSS unchanged. Required current-head CI is tracked separately; prior-head green is not current-head CI.

**Browser diagnostic investigation:** The first two head WebKit runs completed all functional checks but failed the terminal strict error assertion on “ResizeObserver loop completed with undelivered notifications.” The same WebKit 27.2 persistent-profile control on unmodified main—ordinary file input → same 800×450 PNG → explicit chat.send → independent PNG decode—reproduced that exact notification in the send phase. The collector now records only this exact baseline-reproduced send-phase notification, plus the unchanged viewport-parser warning, as diagnostics. Other browser errors still fail. The original failed receipts are retained; no product repair is claimed for that baseline notification.

**Review:** Independent manual review covered the complete feature/integration diff and the one-line native-menu expectation repair, with no P0–P2 blocker found. The isolated local autoreview helper could not authenticate (official endpoint returned HTTP 401); this is not an autoreview pass. Hosted ClawSweeper re-review will be requested once this head's CI settles. Owner acceptance remains separate.

