## What Problem This Solves

Fixes chat attachment cards showing percent-encoded names or storage UUID suffixes when a filename comes from an inbound URI in persisted history or an assistant `MEDIA:` directive.

Closes #185365

## Why This Change Was Made

Persisted history attachments and assistant `MEDIA:` directives now share the same filename-label logic. It decodes one path layer and strips the managed storage UUID while preserving literal percent sequences, malformed escapes, encoded separators, explicit filenames, and the media URI.

## User Impact

