### Live LINE proof

I applied the same change as this PR to the released **2026.9.6** LINE plugin (its built `dist` chunks, edited by hand: `outbound-message-log`, the startup probe hook, the webhook `destination` pass-through, and the awaited record) and ran it against a real LINE channel and Gateway. This is a hand port to the shipped build, not the PR head itself. The proof build also had two temporary `[line-proof]` log lines (whether startup learned the bot user id, and where a quote check matched); they are not part of this PR. The original files were restored afterwards.

Group with mention required (the default `requireMention`, no LINE-specific config added). IDs, names, and message text are omitted; times are local.

| Step | What happened | Log / state |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start | Gateway restarted with the ported build | `[line-proof] startup bot user id known=true account=default`, then `[line] [default] starting LINE provider` |
| Control: pre-fix message | A quote, without mention, of a bot message sent **before** the ported build | `quote check: matched=false source=none` → no reply (that id was never persisted) |
| 1 | User mentions the bot; the bot replies (15:47) | one new row in the bot's `sent-messages.<hash>` namespace at 15:47:50 |
| 2 | **Gateway restarted** (16:54, new process) | `[line-proof] startup bot user id known=true`, `starting LINE provider` |
| 3 | User quotes the bot's 15:47 reply **without a mention** (17:18) | `quote check: matched=true source=plugin-state destinationKnown=true destinationMatchesBot=true` → LINE group session gets a user turn at 17:18:36 and an assistant turn at 17:18:43 → the reply's id is persisted at 17:18:43 and the reply shows in LINE |
| Control: not the bot's message | User quotes **their own** message without a mention (17:19) | `quote check: matched=false source=none`, then `line: drop no mention` → no reply |
| Control: `quotedBot` disabled | `channels.defaults.implicitMentions.quotedBot: false` (hot reload, LINE provider restarted in-process), then the user quotes a bot reply without a mention (next morning) | `quote check: matched=true source=memory`, but the event is not admitted: no LINE session turn, no new sent-id row, no reply |

The match in step 3 came from plugin state (`source=plugin-state`): the in-memory log was empty after the restart, so before this change this quote would have been dropped as "no mention". The test config was removed afterwards.

Not covered live: a quote of a *different* bot's message in the same group (the group had no other bot). The unit and restart tests cover the different-bot and re-pointed-account cases.

